\p{Reading. Instruction counts repeat to 0.3 \% for the machine and 1.2 \% for the reference engine between a run inside a window and a run of the same cell in a suite (section 2); CPU seconds and wall clock are single runs, and two identical 8-worker runs on this host differ by up to 5 \% (J1.md, section 1), so "-6 \%" against "-12 \%" of wall clock between two PGO images is not a finding - "PGO is faster than CE by about a tenth" is. Peak RSS is 7 to 11 \% higher with the Oracle images for the machine (4.3 to 4.4 GiB against 4.0) and lower for the reference engine (5.4 to 6.4 against 7.5 GiB). The Oracle image without a profile shows both, so it is not the profile; the two GraalVM versions differ (25.0.4 against 25.5.5.0.3).}
}

