\p{The whole \code{\verb~|build.sh --pgo~} run of variant A (Maven, CE image, Oracle jars, instrumented image, training on Std + cedar, PGO image, verification of every launcher) took 517 s. Building the PGO image from profiles that already exist is no slower than building the CE image (113 to 193 s of wall clock for the first four, on a host that was loaded differently from build to build, and 610 to 750 CPU seconds, against 125 s and 990 CPU seconds): what costs is the instrumented image (164 s) and the training (21 s for Init, 119 s for Mathlib), and they are needed only when the profile is made. The PGO binary is 47 MB, the CE binary 68 MB, Oracle's without a profile 76 MB (69 MB without its branch-probability model).}
}

\subtree{
\title{1.6 Correctness: the arena's 270 tests}

\p{\strong{Oracle GraalVM - measurement only, not a default build.} The arena's complete test set (270 tests: 148 good incl. the eight corpora, 92 bad, 30 either) by the arena's procedure: one arena-shaped container per row, tests one after the other, the arena's time limit per test, \code{\verb~|perf stat~} around the run line.}

